    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "A ship sails 32 kilometres north and then 24 kilometres east. How far is it from its starting point?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$40\\text{ km}$",
      "worked": "North and east are perpendicular, so the direct distance is the hypotenuse. Let $d$ be the distance from the starting point, in kilometres.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}d^2&=32^2+24^2\\\\d^2&=1024+576\\\\d^2&=1600\\\\d&=40\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe ship is $40\\text{ km}$ from its starting point.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
